monitor: MON or WOZ [line]  then:  addr  addr.addr
         addr:b b b  addrR  X leaves
files:   DIR [A] [dir|pattern]
         (DIR PRG lists it; DIR *.PAS, DIR ?.TXT
         match here; * any run, ? any one)
         CD [dir]
         MKDIR dir
         RM name
         RMDIR dir
         TYPE name
         XD name
         LOAD name [addr]
         SAVE name from.to
         RENAME old new
         CP old new
         RUN [name.prg|addr]
         EXEC script  (a # line is a comment)
         (bare names search the language dirs)
         an unknown word runs name.prg from disk, with
         args (ARGS call $FF95)
         names starting with . are hidden from DIR
         (DIR A shows them)
memory:  FILL from.to value
         COPY from.to dest
system:  INFO
         TIME
         MODE [0-2] [0|1]
         COLOR fg [bg]
         ECHO
         CLS
         CLG (clear the bitmap; *CLG in a BASIC)
         ALIAS [name [text]]
         (ALIAS lists; ALIAS LL DIR A defines;
         ALIAS LL with nothing after it removes.
         Kept in RAM: define them in STARTUP.BAT)
         HUSH
         RESET
         CAPSLOCK [ON|OFF]
         (toggle; letters typed come up uppercase --
         *CAPSLOCK in a BASIC)
         DUMP [note|ON|OFF]
tongues: BBC (BBC BASIC on the Tube)
         CPM (CP/M 2.2, the Z80 second processor)
         FORTH (Tali Forth 2, native)
         EHBASIC
         Mad Pascal: cross-compiled .prg files
         (pascal/): PMANDEL PSIEVE HELLO
network: a URL is a file name (Meatloaf):
         TYPE http://host/file
         CP http://host/x.prg x.prg
         RUN http://host/x.prg
         LOAD "http://..." in EhBASIC and BBC BASIC
         CD tnfs://host/dir puts the current directory
         on a TNFS server (FujiNet, Meatloaf):
         DIR lists it, bare names load from it,
         CD .. climbs,
         CD - comes home
         TELNET host port (F12 hangs up)
         on the N: device at $D900; ANSI/VT100 via JIM
terminal: JIM at $DA00, a VT100/ANSI in hardware:
         CP/M programs and BBC BASIC draw through it
         (install CP/M programs for VT100 or ANSI);
         TELNET too
host:    F7 opens the settings menu
         (border, font, volume, keys, reset);
         Super+PgUp resets
boot:    /STARTUP.BAT runs as an EXEC script at
         power-on; hold a key to skip it
